   "body": "### Motivation\n- The Schwartz-Zippel step in `lem:qld-xz-lines` resamples a point on a sampled line by a uniform affine parameter. Issue #452 tracks the unconditional mixed-law identity needed for that step; see `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:950-955` and `def:line-point-dist` at paper section 08, lines 274-287.\n\n### Description\n- Add `avgOver_linePointDist_resample_parameter` for the equal mixture of axis and diagonal line-point distributions.\n- Derive the result from the published axis and diagonal identities through `avgOver_mix`, preserving zero-direction diagonal fibers and adding no hypotheses.\n- Re-export the new module from `MIPStarRE.QPBT.Combining.Lines`.\n\n### Testing\n- `lake build MIPStarRE.QPBT.Combining.Lines.MixedResampling`\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/MixedResampling.lean`\n- `lake build MIPStarRE.QPBT.Combining.Lines`\n- Proof-hole and forbidden-bypass scan of the new module\n- `#print axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.avgOver_linePointDist_resample_parameter` (`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` only)\n- `scripts/install_git_hooks.sh --check`\n\n---\nCloses #452\n",
