-  "body": "### Motivation\n\n- Recover the already-proved honest QPBT strategy for #156 on the current public\n  interfaces, preserving current sampler, distribution, and symmetry proofs.\n- The paper statement is `lem:pauli-completeness`,\n  `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1229-1421`.\n\n### Description\n\n- Prove the unchanged `exists_spcc_value_one (P : AdmissibleParams)` by the\n  concrete honest measurement family on all 26 question types. The proof\n  establishes SPCC, correct line answers, zero malformed effects, and zero\n  rejected Born weight. No additional hypothesis or proof hole is introduced.\n- Recover the four saved honest-strategy support files and only the final\n  constructor/proof section of `Completeness.lean`. The existing 7,990-character\n  sampler/distribution/symmetry prefix is byte-identical.\n- Reuse exactly PR207's published 83-line Pauli projector patch. Expose only\n  six existing mathematical helper proofs without changing their hypotheses or\n  bodies; use existing public projectivity, relabeling, and tensor APIs.\n- nts, receipts and tickets were inspected read-only; no live admission test or floor-eight/replacement claim is made. Independent review and deployment remain pending.\n\n---\nAddresses #257\n",
